#use(std/html)

#section{Raw HTML escape hatch}::

This page lives outside the handbook on purpose: #tt{std/html} emits raw
nodes only the HTML backend accepts, so a document using it #emph{cannot}
render to typst (the backend errors rather than dropping content — the
tests assert exactly that). Keep raw HTML in leaf documents you only ever
build as HTML.

Inline form, for phrasing content the IR has no element for:
#html{<abbr title="Yet Another Markup Dialect">YAMD</abbr>} stays a working
#tt{<abbr>}.

Block form, for flow content — #tt{##html-block} is a raw body, so tags,
braces and #tt{##} are all literal:

#html-block
	<details>
		<summary>Why not extend the IR instead?</summary>
		<p>Usually you should — a plugin emitting portable elements works in
		every backend. The escape hatch is for the rest.</p>
	</details>
